== Features ==
- add hostname, pid, tid (all optional)
- per-logger params - are these inherited transitively? Yes, probably by traversing log ancestors, but could also keep a local cache
- time to go through and review/cleanup/rebase: approach public repo state
  - might make sense to convert tests to more TEST_CASE-based

static fields: toggle with flags:
enum class Fields {
  File = 1,
  Line = 2,
  Time = 4,
  Level = 8,
  LevelName = 16,
  LogName = 32,
  ProcessName = 64, // assume static
  ProcessId = 128, // assume static
  ThreadId = 256, // maaaaybe static?
  Hostname = 512, // assume static
};

Logger params: implicit level 0 (always included in messages)


== Separate logsink lib == 
- Expected log messages (if this occurs it is not an error. If it does not occur, that is an error (useful for testing)
- buffering: copy messages to memory buffer. If a message of severity X occurs, flush buffer
